    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0290" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00 Revolutions/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-03T16:00:00-06:00">December 3, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:07 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>100. Gomez Zarate and Enrique Cordova were at revolutionary headquarters this
                    morning. General Claramount was arrested last night by the police but the
                        latter<anchor n="3" xml:id="d187-f1"/> surrendered this morning. President
                    Araujo refuses the demands of the revolutionists, of which the only important
                    one is his resignation. The plan of the revolutionists is to put the Vice
                    President in but no doubt he will be forced out as quickly as possible, but he
                    probably does not have much desire for the office anyhow. President promised his
                    truce until 10 a.m. tomorrow, and I believe the revolutionists will accept it
                    for they have more to gain by delay than he has. [Paraphrase.] Those named were
                    very probably back of the revolution, and I think that the last named was one of
                    the leaders.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d187-f2"/> [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d187-f1" n="3" xml:id="d187-f1-content">
                <p>i. e., the police.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d187-f2" n="4" xml:id="d187-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 105, December 4, 1 p.m., <ref target="#pg172">p. 172</ref>, and
                    pars. 4 and 5 of despatch No. 26, December 15, from the Minister in El Salvador,
                        <ref target="#pg197">p. 197</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
